WEBVTT

00:00:00.550 --> 00:00:09.838
Let's follow two workers as they ask for five days of work. You'll see what to do on the phone, and what the office does on the computer.

00:00:12.038 --> 00:00:15.614
Every name and date you see is for practice.

00:00:18.717 --> 00:00:27.213
Use the download link below the video. Choose Android for your phone, or Windows or Linux for your computer.

00:00:30.342 --> 00:00:33.870
On the computer, start with Sign in with Google.

00:00:37.008 --> 00:00:45.984
On Select login area, choose your State and Financial Year. The Financial Year is the year for these work records.

00:00:48.184 --> 00:00:53.968
Then choose your District and Block. Check that all four choices are right.

00:00:56.168 --> 00:00:59.360
Click Save and open login page.

00:01:02.467 --> 00:01:09.523
Sign in to the work website with your own account. You enter the Security Code and choose Login.

00:01:12.633 --> 00:01:17.745
Open My Areas to keep your usual Panchayats and Villages together.

00:01:19.945 --> 00:01:25.201
When records need to be read, the app starts with the area you are using.

00:01:28.342 --> 00:01:35.878
The office sets up phone access under Android access. Get your private login code from the office.

00:01:39.008 --> 00:01:44.288
On the phone, check your area. Tap Create work request.

00:01:46.488 --> 00:01:51.504
Find the workers who asked for work. Tick one name at a time.

00:01:54.633 --> 00:02:01.113
Both workers want five days. Type five in Days for all selected workers.

00:02:03.313 --> 00:02:09.505
Tap Apply Days to All. Check that both workers now show five days.

00:02:12.633 --> 00:02:14.505
Tap Continue.

00:02:16.705 --> 00:02:18.817
Choose the Start Date.

00:02:21.017 --> 00:02:23.537
Then open Review request.

00:02:26.675 --> 00:02:31.619
Check the names, days, and dates. Tap Send to office.

00:02:33.819 --> 00:02:39.387
Open History to see the request. The office still needs to check it.

00:02:43.342 --> 00:02:48.790
On the computer, open Work Demand. Choose Received requests.

00:02:50.990 --> 00:02:57.398
Open a request. Read the names, requested days, and start dates.

00:03:00.508 --> 00:03:05.500
Click Check demand. Read the result before you do anything else.

00:03:07.700 --> 00:03:12.476
If a worker needs a closer look, read the reason beside their name.

00:03:15.592 --> 00:03:20.968
You can also start a request on the computer. Choose Create demand.

00:03:23.168 --> 00:03:28.376
Check the Financial Year. Then choose your Panchayat and Village.

00:03:31.508 --> 00:03:34.820
Open Workers and tick the names you want.

00:03:37.191 --> 00:03:40.695
You can use Worker filters to narrow the list.

00:03:43.800 --> 00:03:50.760
Add a Work Code or Work Order if you need one. These tell the app which work you mean.

00:03:52.960 --> 00:03:56.896
If the Work step is optional, you can leave it blank.

00:04:00.008 --> 00:04:08.672
Open Days and dates. The Application Date is when the workers asked for work. Check that date first.

00:04:10.872 --> 00:04:17.088
Enter five in No of Days. Use Start Date for the first day the workers want to work.

00:04:19.288 --> 00:04:24.376
The app shows the End Date. Read it, then click Check demand.

00:04:28.342 --> 00:04:33.358
Use Print Demand if you want a draft copy for review or printing.

00:04:35.558 --> 00:04:42.422
A draft copy lets you review the names, days, and dates before official entry.

00:04:45.550 --> 00:04:53.926
Read the checked list. In the real office workflow, Send to VBGRAMG starts official entry.

00:04:56.126 --> 00:05:02.534
Watch the progress. You may still have to press a final Submit button on the work website.

00:05:05.675 --> 00:05:14.171
Look at these two counts. Two entry steps finished. The app could confirm only one saved demand.

00:05:16.371 --> 00:05:22.035
When a result is unclear, check the saved list before trying to send it again.

00:05:26.008 --> 00:05:32.296
Open Reports for Muster Rolls. A Muster Roll is the worker attendance list.

00:05:34.496 --> 00:05:38.264
Choose the Panchayat and the Villages you want.

00:05:41.383 --> 00:05:46.471
Choose the groups to include. Use Generate to make the PDF.

00:05:49.592 --> 00:05:54.536
In Settings you can change the look of the app and manage saved records.

00:05:56.736 --> 00:06:01.032
Open Balance and recharges to see your balance.

00:06:04.133 --> 00:06:11.597
Open the practice app below the video. Pick two workers, enter five days, and click Check demand.

00:06:13.797 --> 00:06:18.069
Take your time. You can replay any lesson.
